<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO's EAB Q2 net income falls.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO's EAB Q2 net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter 1997</p>
<p>(millions of dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net income			     28.91   vs  34.50</p>
<p>    Net interest income		  95.16   vs  86.39</p>
<p>    Provision for loan losses	   3.00   vs   6.00</p>
<p>    Other operating income	     20.82   vs  20.49</p>
<p>    Other operating expenses	   65.88   vs  62.92</p>
<p>    Tax					18.19   vs   3.46</p>
<p>NOTE - EAB, a full-service bank for the New York area, is a fully-owned U.S unit of Dutch ABN AMRO Bank NV. It said the fall in net income was due to a higher effective level of taxation.</p>
<p>SIX MONTHS TO JUNE 30</p>
<p>    Net income			     57.08   vs  65.71</p>
<p>    Net interest income		 190.87   vs 169.50</p>
<p>    Provision for loan losses	   7.50   vs  13.50</p>
<p>    Other operating income	     42.87   vs  40.41</p>
<p>    Other operating expenses	  133.24   vs 124.51</p>
<p>    Tax					35.91   vs   6.19</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
